# Format at End of Task

Run the formatter **once, when the task is complete** — not after every individual edit.

## Scope

Format **only files you changed** in this task. Do not run a repo-wide format.

### Changed files only

```bash
pnpm exec biome format --write path/to/changed-file.ts path/to/other.tsx
```

### Package scope (when all changes live in one package)

If every changed file is under the same `packages/<name>/`, format that package:

```bash
pnpm --filter @m4trix/tracing format
pnpm --filter @m4trix/trace-viewer format
pnpm --filter @m4trix/core format
```

Use package format when multiple files in one package changed; use explicit paths when changes are scattered or at the repo root.

## When to run

- Once, before marking the task done
- After implementation/tests, as a final cleanup step
- Skip if you did not modify any formattable source files

## Do not

- Run `pnpm format` at the repo root (formats the entire monorepo)
- Re-format on every intermediate edit
- Format unrelated packages or untouched files

This project uses **Biome** (`biome.json`). Do not use Prettier for formatting.
